**Q-6, provisional (harness era).** Strategy D(B), pooled stacks with
software probes and decommit on park; default reservation 1 MiB, which passes
section 2.4 at 100k and 1M tasks on M1 and M3, the two machines with 16 GiB
(w = {{ w(M1, "D(B)/1M") }} and {{ w(M3, "D(B)/1M") }}; M2 confirms it at 100k, and
128 KiB passes on all three); probes, not guard pages; `spawn` ambient,
without a capability; the stackless fallback is not needed. Section 9 gives
the reasons and the conditions.

## 0. Provenance

Policy of record: the owner's answers in the README's "Policy decisions"
section (machines may be virtual or GitHub-hosted runners; default sysctls; Go
after its garbage collection as the memory baseline; D(B) as the default
strategy; a 5 KiB probe reserve; the 1M-after-excursion cell required only of
page-releasing strategies; compiler-inserted yield points with their cost in
the probe budget). Section 10.1 lists what they changed in the plan.

